WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.090
What are you doing, Yamato-kun?

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:08.070
I told you. I'm here for revenge.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.530
"Get back my song."

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.370
I won't forgive anyone who 
encroaches on Zero's territory.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.250
Yamato-kun, what are you talking about?

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.920
I agreed to act in that 
movie so I could do this.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.460
My goal was for you to let your guard down.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.880
Did you write all that graffiti 
at Takanashi Productions, too?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.260
That's right!

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.720
You think you can cover Zero's song?

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:43.710
I'm punishing you for your arrogance!

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.730
Yamato-kun, you...

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.720
Serves you right!

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.460
Now Momo will never sing again.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.510
Pretty great fifth anniversary, right?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.780
Don't be ridiculous!

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.880
If Momo loses his voice, 
I'll never forgive you!

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:07.250
I was able to keep making music 
because I had him by my side.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.960
As far as I'm concerned, 
Momo is a better singer than Zero!

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.590
Yuki, is that true?

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.090
What?

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.100
It's <i>obviously</i> true!

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.490
Right, Yuki-san?

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.730
Aren't you glad you got to hear what 
Yuki-san really thinks, Momo-san?

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:30.150
Look. He got all worked up over you, too.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:32.490
Huh? What?

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.300
Can we move on now?

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.950
Please let go of me, Senpai.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.490
Yamato-kun, you were poisoning 
Momo, weren't you?

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.290
Wait a second... it was all an act?

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.590
Re:vale Prank Successful!!

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.530
Prank successful!

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:56.300
You said yourself that
 I'm a prodigious actor, remember?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.520
But you fell for it hook, line, and sinker.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.020
Hilarious.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.890
Momo, did you know about this?

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.730
They just told me.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.900
Yuki, I'm so happy.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.400
I could feel how much you love me!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.900
I'm so embarrassed!

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.750
Don't worry. You're super handsome!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.890
Actually, we have another surprise for you.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:23.410
What?

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.410
There's more?

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.660
Please come in, Banri.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:29.920
Banri?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.570
Hello.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:38.920
Was the prank a success?

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.750
Ban...

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.940
Ban-san?

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.300
It's Ban-san!

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.370
It's good to see you again, Yuki.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:47.140
You really shouldn't trouble 
Momo-kun like that.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.020
You...

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.640
It's because you suddenly disappeared!

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.280
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.820
Sorry for making you worry.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.610
President Takanashi took me in.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.790
I work at their agency now.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.400
We were surprised, too.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.500
We had no idea Banri-san
was actually your partner.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.910
Ban, how's your injury?

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:15.950
Do you have a scar?

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.800
It's mostly faded now.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.260
See? You can't tell when 
it's hidden behind my bangs.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.640
Are you happy?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:30.310
Yeah. I don't sing anymore, 
but I'm enjoying every day.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.930
Thanks to these boys, IDOLiSH7.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:35.900
Banri-san.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.120
I've been rooting for Re:vale, too.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.900
<b>Re:vale Three-peats at <i>Black or White</i></b>

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.900
Congratulations on winning 
the <i>Black or White</i>,

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.410
and on your fifth anniversary.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.390
You've been watching us?

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.290
Of course I have.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.620
I've always supported you, too, Momo-kun.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.990
I was a fan of yours, Ban-san.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.420
I always wondered if it was 
okay for me to take the place

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.360
of the man I admired,
and work by Yuki-san's side.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.640
What are you talking about?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.880
Of course it's okay.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.180
Ban-san.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.020
Because of you, Yuki kept making music.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:10.790
I'm grateful to you.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.180
Thank you, Momo-kun.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.260
You don't need to thank me!

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.980
Ban, you don't resent me?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.120
You were injured protecting me,

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.380
but only I went on to be successful.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.230
Don't insult me.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:28.160
Is that the kind of guy you think I am?

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.120
No! No, I—

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.630
I know.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.870
You've been singing for me, too, haven't you?

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:40.580
I didn't want to erase the Re:vale 
we created together.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.910
Re:vale belongs to you and Momo-kun now.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:44.580
Ban.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.380
Ban-san.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.610
The current Re:vale is the true Re:vale.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.640
Hold your heads high.
Don't doubt yourselves anymore.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.240
I'll be cheering for you 
louder than anyone else.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:01.070
So be confident in yourselves. 
Let me hear you sing.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.400
I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:04.510
Yeah.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.300
We will.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.870
I'm glad we got to see Ban-san, Yuki.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:12.660
Yeah.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.290
They brought him here for us.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.670
They're such good boys.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.170
You're right. We've been 
blessed with good juniors.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:26.030
Now it's our turn to be 
good examples for them.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:26.740
Yeah.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.050
Yuki-san, Momo-san!

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.430
We're going on now!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.950
Hold on a second.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:33.790
Yamato-kun.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:34.290
Huh?

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:39.360
Did you really think you'd be able to 
perform without any kind of punishment?

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.480
Punishment?

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.740
Deceiving your kind senior 
is a serious crime.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.490
Goodbye, Yama-san.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.460
Huh? What are you—

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:48.990
Oh, my God.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:53.490
Will you kindly hear the kind 
request of your kind senior?

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.830
Come on, Yamato-kun. Lead the group.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.010
Why me?

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:04.460
Isn't this Yaotome's job?

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.470
It's fine. You can have the honors today.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:11.260
Show us how you do it, Leader.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.640
That's right, Leader.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.690
We're counting on you, Leader.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.370
Hurry up, Leader.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.100
Fight on, Leader!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.630
Please, Leader.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.900
You can do it, Leader!

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.110
You guys will pay for this.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.360
Anyway, this is a big moment for our seniors.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:33.990
If we're to return double what we received, 
there's only one thing we can do.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.660
Let's give this everything we've got!

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.080
Let's go!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.830
Yeah!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:56.390
<i>New Zero Arena Three Days Limited 
Fifth Anniversary Live! Start!</i>

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.690
What? TRIGGER and i7?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.810
No way. Why?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.510
Are they the opening act?

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:11.080
What a treat.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.460
This song...

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.650
It's ours.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.650
Seriously?

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:39.410
They're going to make me 
cry with their surprise.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:44.140
I see. That's why they wanted 
to make this the opening act.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:44.670
Huh?

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.060
It's a message to you.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:48.920
What?

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:53.400
Our songs contain five years' 
worth of memories.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.930
Our debut song, our drama and 
regular TV show theme songs,

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:02.430
our commercial theme songs, the songs 
we received from artists we admire.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.460
All of them make up the trail we left behind.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.440
You're right.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:09.650
They're memories of singing by your side.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.680
You and I have worked as 
Re:vale this whole time.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.310
You're my partner.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:17.160
Yuki.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.690
Get on standby, please.

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:20.500
Sure.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.150
Momo-kun, how are you feeling?

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:23.110
We can prep the vocal track—

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.090
That won't be necessary.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.660
Yuki.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.580
You can sing, can't you?

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:30.470
Yeah, I can.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.430
I can sing!

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.460
Okay!

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.420
Let's go.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.220
Yeah.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.210
Momo!

00:09:58.210 --> 00:09:59.780
Yuki-san!

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.550
Yuki!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.070
Momo!

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.210
Yuki!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.990
Yuki-sama!

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:13.570
Thank you, Zero Arena.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.370
We are Re:vale!

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.610
Momo!

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:19.870
Let's have an awesome night together.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:22.690
Yuki!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.070
Listen to this.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:29.450
The song TRIGGER and IDOLiSH7 just 
sang was actually a surprise.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.130
I thought, "Hey, I've heard this song before."

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.120
"It's a good song."

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.190
Don't call your own songs good.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:40.300
They sang Re:vale songs filled with
 memories of Yuki and me.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:45.840
Whether I'm happy or sad, 
I've got Yuki, all our fans,

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.710
and all the agency employees and staff.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.100
I've been blessed with cute juniors, too.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.520
Thanks to all of you, I made it this far.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:00.850
I worked really hard these past five years.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.350
And I'll keep on working even harder!

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.700
I love Re:vale.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:12.910
I'll continue delivering the 
ultimate Re:vale to all of you.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:15.360
With five years' worth of gratitude...

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.990
This is Re:vale's "Dis One."!

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.680
The world is so dazzling, my eyes can't take it

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:49.190
Dizzy... spark and dark, I closed my eyes

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:55.290
"How long are you staying desperate?"
I'm afraid of the answer

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:59.470
Unknown... so I played dumb

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:01.210
Momo-san's singing live.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:05.870
Even so, for the hopes that I can't lose

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:02.030
That's great.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.170
Congratulations!

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:03.760
Yeah.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:05.870
Shit!

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:06.900
What is it?

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.920
I jump into a struggle

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:08.920
That wizard ran up the stairs.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.660
Has he come to interfere with the concert?

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:14.650
I can't wait till my wounds heal

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.410
Wait. We should call security to—

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.920
Jeez, they're so hot-blooded!

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:20.040
I surpassed yesterday's
version of myself, Dis one.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.170
Hold it!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.010
You're not getting away.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:25.930
Step over and create another new This one.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:32.120
When looking at it from
the future, yes, "now" is hope

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.430
He ran downstairs!

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:30.370
Let's split up.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.770
We'll circle around to the loading bay side.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:37.230
Are you Alright? I won't give up yet

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:33.350
Got it!

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.400
You shouldn't run!

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.440
I'll be fine.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.860
You can't. This is why you keep triggering—

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:42.650
Over! Over! Now... Break Dis one!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:40.930
Shut up!

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:43.140
You're not my family anymore!

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.170
Huh? Uh...

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:50.120
Rikkun, I'll handle this!

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:51.860
Tamaki-kun!

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.400
Oh, Tamaki!

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:57.280
Why is it so freezing in the light?

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.790
You're so fast!

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.960
Stop!

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.470
Riku, take the stage door.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:03.130
Oh... my pain, I learned solitude

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.060
We'll descend from the gate side.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:01.080
Got it.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.380
So you'll listen to other people.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:08.380
"If I stop, I'll only fall"
the rule I set is binding me

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.430
It's because you treat me like a child.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.380
Wait!

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:13.490
Egoistic, where's the exit?

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.160
You're the one who said 
we weren't family first.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:20.170
I want someone to recognize
me... No, that's not it

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.080
It's not fair for you to act hurt now.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.570
What I'm searching for

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:28.660
Yes, it's always beyond that

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:33.980
No matter how fancy you decorate the world

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.980
Nowhere else to run now.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.240
Show your face.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:39.720
That's not enough to ensure "now" anymore

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.290
Are you the real Zero?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:42.380
If you're really him, why don't you
 stand onstage and sing again?

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:46.230
If this place is Pandora's box,
the only hope that remains

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.340
Why—

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.120
<b>Inside</b>

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.120
<b>Inside</b>

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.120
<b>Outside</b>

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.340
<b>Outside</b>

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.340
<b>Outside</b>

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:46.230
Whoa!

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.280
Are you okay, Mikki?!

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:50.910
We still OK, that's right... Is inside me

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.590
Damn! Get the lights!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.910
He's gone.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.610
This way.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:55.930
Revive! Revive! Come on...
Now, our dream will face Rebirth!

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.560
He ran towards the parking lot!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.920
He's not here.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.940
He can't reach the stage from the basement.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.860
Did he give up on interfering?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.420
Let's contact security.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.860
His clothes make him stand out.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:05.690
I bet they'll find him.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.470
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:16.370
Every time I reach something,
back to point zero, I Turn

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:20.790
But that's not the end

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:27.670
Let's stand up and face it,
we will... over and over

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:32.970
I surpassed yesterday's
version of myself, Dis one.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:38.660
Step over and create another new This one.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:44.860
When looking at it from
the future, yes, "now" is hope

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:49.400
Are you Alright? I won't give up yet

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:54.990
Over! Over! Now... Break Dis one!

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.970
Thank you, everyone.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:20.310
We sang out of gratitude for the restoration 
of this stage and to thank Zero

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.230
for turning this stage into a legend.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:27.870
I feel blessed to have sung Zero's 
song with Yuki on this stage.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.440
We hope you'll continue to support Re:vale.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.880
No, thank you!

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.170
We'd better thank them, too.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:41.580
Yeah. TRIGGER and IDOLiSH7!

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.000
What?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.500
Let's go. Come on.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.280
TRIGGER!

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.010
IDOLiSH7!

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:52.790
Let's hear it for TRIGGER and IDOLiSH7.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.020
No, thank you.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.320
Congratulations on your fifth anniversary.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.060
Thanks, everyone!

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:09.070
Congratulations on the opening 
of the remodeled Zero Arena.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:13.720
I hope many more legends 
are born on this stage.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:18.180
Now, let's build today's legend together!

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.830
The fun's just getting started!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.300
Once again, cheers!

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.800
Cheers!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.530
Great job, everyone.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.930
Let's get this afterparty started!

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:39.220
<b>Momo  Yuki 
Yaotome Gaku   Tenn   Ryu</b>

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:39.220
All right!

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.220
No, don't!

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.230
Are you listening? Before 
<i>Cocona</i>, there was...

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.810
I was so surprised!

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.520
I wasn't expecting you guys 
to sing a medley of our songs.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:54.460
We secretly planned it 
and practiced together.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.070
It was worth it.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.440
I was touched.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.500
I'm glad we have such great juniors.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.290
Well, Re:vale's done a lot for us.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.770
You were awesome.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.920
Momo-san, your voice sounded great.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:06.920
Thanks!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:11.210
We'll keep looking after our 
precious little juniors.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:16.250
First, Yamato-kun, 
let's talk about our movie.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:19.740
I'm going to prank you
 thirty times during filming.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.390
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.930
Today's main dish has arrived!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.870
It's the traditional lunch boxes
 we've been waiting for.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.810
Oh, wonderful!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:35.690
You guys always eat good stuff.

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:36.930
Not at all.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:41.370
It was a long, hard road to get here.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:42.190
Really?

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:42.950
I dunno.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.930
Ban, let me get your contact info.

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.710
Sure, but why?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.890
Why? You can't be serious.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:53.320
Come on. Let me take 
a picture for your profile.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.110
Look this way.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.290
What? You haven't even set
 a photo for <i>me</i>, though.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.190
Yeah, sure. I will, right after this.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:00.180
Ban, come on.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.850
Yuki, you're being creepy.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.240
He called you a creep.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.480
I've been looking at the same 
photo albums for five years.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.100
<b>That's what you've been doing?</b>

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.100
How could you say that to me?

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.000
Sorry.

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:13.610
Wanna drink? Don't be shy.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:17.740
Come on. Drink up before the foam spills.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.290
I love TRIGGER's dance moves!

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.290
C'mon!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:22.730
Tsunashi-san!

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:23.860
Tenn, drink up.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.640
Don't be shy.

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:26.040
What?

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.050
Hang on, jeez...

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:30.290
Hey, Ryu! Tenn's underage!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.920
I've always thought you 
were a good guy, Gaku.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.640
You're handsome, honest, 
and like a little brother.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.140
Okay, okay.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.220
Okay, fisherman.

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.370
Tenn-nii, where are you going?

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:46.800
To get changed.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:51.240
Good. It seems like he's 
not mad about earlier.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.140
What happened earlier?

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:53.940
I actually—

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.630
Mitsuki, your face is red.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:58.530
Not at all. I'm not drunk at all.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.610
Are you okay, Nii-san?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.800
I'm fine.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.780
Mitsuki's tolerance is lower than mine.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.910
Nagi, you've drank alcohol before?

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:11.630
Yes. In my country, the drinking age is 16.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.230
You can't drink in Japan, though.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.660
I'm not drinking.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:18.920
If I seem drunk, honey,

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.800
it's because your charms—

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:21.690
Ouch!

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:23.560
Hey, you're in the way.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.360
Could you watch where you're going,
like in every single direction?

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:27.800
Sorry.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.560
The bread we received was so good.

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.690
Huh? When did this get here?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.580
"Thanks for singing my song."

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:42.450
"From Zero"?

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:43.950
Zero?!

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.030
Dramatic surprise!

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.080
It's like magic.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.770
That's great.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.670
If he gave you that message, 
it means he's not mad.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:03.840
Then, who was the Zero who appeared at 
the press conference and tonight's concert?

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:07.000
Just a fanatic who's behind the times.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.070
Are you awake, Kujo-san?

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:20.980
Tenn.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:23.480
You should rest for now.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:26.520
Don't think. Just rest.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.080
You're right.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:33.300
I had a nostalgic dream.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.250
I dreamed Zero was singing at Zero Arena.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:43.090
Back when just supporting him made me happy.

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:47.710
I know, Kujo-san.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.860
Your real dream isn't to surpass Zero.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:59.870
You want Zero so badly, you're 
unconsciously becoming him.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:07.770
Tenn-nii.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:10.410
Riku.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.830
Where are Kujo and Aya-chan?

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:17.250
They left Japan so Aya 
could continue her lessons.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.260
I see.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:24.220
I've thought a lot about what you 
said, but I won't quit being an idol.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.650
I may still be inexperienced,

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:30.350
but I'll do my best to become 
an idol you'll acknowledge.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:33.540
And when I do, you'd better buy tickets.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:34.640
Tickets?

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.070
To IDOLiSH7's concert.

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:39.360
It's a promise to do your best with a smile.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.440
That's what you said.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.480
Discover...

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.690
Once you think I'm an idol 
who can keep his promises,

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:46.740
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.740
I want you to buy a ticket and come see me.

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:49.570
I promise I'll turn you into one of my fans.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:48.700
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:54.720
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.060
Wow...

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:10.590
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:16.010
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:20.420
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:26.020
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:28.890
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:31.430
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:36.680
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:38.540
Discover...

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:42.440
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:47.750
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:49.200
Night sky

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:53.340
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:55.540
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:22:55.540 --> 00:23:01.440
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.740
Wow...

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:20.710
<i>New Zero Arena inaugural concert.</i>

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.060
Three Days Extra<i>, now on sale.</i>

00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:27.420
Re:vale, TRIGGER, and IDOLiSH7 
have all been getting along great

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:29.010
since before the inaugural concert.

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:29.840
I know.

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:32.840
I hope they stay friends 
as they move ahead.

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:34.510
I know what you mean.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:38.470
Friends forever, huh?

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:41.060
What idiots.

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:43.640
The end is near.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:50.510
And so is yours, Kujo Tenn.

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:55.010
<b>To be continued</b>

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:58.310
<b>Anime "IDOLiSH7"</b>

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:58.310
<b>Season 3 to be produced!</b>
